# The Next.js *app* never imports anything from inside anchor/ at
# runtime (it reads the generated IDL from the repo-root idls/ dir
# instead — see CLAUDE.md's "Monorepo layout") — this is the separate
# Anchor/Solana on-chain program workspace, ~4GB including its own
# target/ and .anchor/ build artifacts. Excluding it isn't just a size
# optimization: anchor/.anchor/test-ledger/admin.rpc is a leftover UNIX
# socket from a local test-validator run, which crashes Vercel's own
# upload/tar step with ENXIO if it's ever included, regardless of
# anchor/.gitignore already covering it.
#
# `anchor/idls/` (104K of plain JSON) is the one exception: `next build`
# type-checks the whole TS project, including `scripts/*.ts` — CLI tools
# never bundled into the deployed app, but still statically imported by
# path — and `scripts/txline-subscribe.ts` imports
# `../anchor/idls/txline.json` directly. `anchor/*` (not bare `anchor`)
# plus the `!anchor/idls` negation is what actually lets that survive:
# gitignore-style negation can't resurrect a path whose parent directory
# was itself excluded.
anchor/*
!anchor/idls

# Not needed at deploy time, and .claude/ specifically holds session
# state, not app source.
.claude
demo-assets
keeper/logs.ndjson
